{"id":"ddc99e2b8879001771d70091e9a4d2b9b7f3c8c9","axis":"silent","repo":"apache/tika","sha":"ddc99e2b8879001771d70091e9a4d2b9b7f3c8c9","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"CHANGES.txt","lines":["@@ -9,6 +9,10 @@ Release 4.3.0 - ???","      last task using it ends) and on graceful shutdown; nothing closed them before.","      EmittingUnpackHandler takes the emitter, not the EmitterManager (TIKA-5001)."," ","+   * tika-grpc refuses SaveFetcher with configStoreType memory (FAILED_PRECONDITION):","+     the forks never saw such a fetcher, so every fetch through it failed. Use file or","+     ignite (TIKA-5001).","+","   SERVER, PIPES AND OPERATIONS"," ","    * The tika-server full and tika-grpc Docker images no longer install","@@ -42,6 +46,11 @@ Release 4.3.0 - ???"," ","   OTHER CHANGES"," ","+   * A runtime fetcher or emitter save or delete reaches running pipes workers at","+     their next fetch, through a change token on file and ignite stores","+     (ConfigStore.changeToken); before, a worker kept the instance it first built","+     until it restarted (TIKA-5001).","+","    * PEM-armored CMS/PKCS7 (-----BEGIN PKCS7----- or -----BEGIN CMS-----) is parsed like","      DER: Pkcs7Parser and the opt-in pkcs-7-detector report the smime-type and extract","      signed content; -----BEGIN CMS----- is now detected (TIKA-5002)."],"additions":9,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/modules/ROOT/pages/pipes/configuration.adoc","lines":["@@ -256,7 +256,7 @@ For multi-host pipelines (e.g., shared-server clusters) you can store fetcher/em"," "," |`configStoreType`"," |`\"memory\"`","-|Backend for storing fetcher/emitter configurations registered at runtime; those in the config file are never written to it. `\"memory\"` (default) is in-process; `\"file\"` persists to a JSON file; `\"ignite\"` uses Apache Ignite for shared state across nodes.","+|Backend for storing fetcher/emitter configurations registered at runtime; those in the config file are never written to it. `\"memory\"` (default) is in-process and not seen by the forked workers; `\"file\"` persists to a JSON file; `\"ignite\"` uses Apache Ignite for shared state across nodes. With `file` or `ignite`, a runtime save or delete reaches running workers at their next fetch."," "," |`configStoreParams`"," |`\"{}\"`"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/modules/ROOT/pages/using-tika/grpc/index.adoc","lines":["@@ -126,11 +126,17 @@ config."," |==="," "," Fetches run in the forked pipes workers, and each worker builds its own config store from the","-same settings. With the default in-memory `configStoreType`, a fetcher saved through","-`SaveFetcher` exists only in the gRPC JVM and every `FetchAndParse` that names it fails with","-`FETCHER_NOT_FOUND`. When `allowComponentManagement` is `true`, set `configStoreType` to `file`","-or `ignite` (see xref:pipes/configuration.adoc#_distributed_config_store[Distributed Config","-Store]) so the workers see the same store.","+same settings. A fetcher saved to the default in-memory `configStoreType` would exist only in the","+gRPC JVM, so `SaveFetcher` is refused with `FAILED_PRECONDITION`. To save fetchers at runtime,","+set `configStoreType` to `file` or `ignite` (see","+xref:pipes/configuration.adoc#_distributed_config_store[Distributed Config Store]) so the","+workers see the same store.","+","+A save or delete takes effect for fetches that start after it, in every worker. A fetch already","+running finishes with the fetcher it started with, even if that fetcher was just deleted or its","+credentials replaced; the old instance is closed when the last such fetch ends. Each fetch through","+a runtime fetcher reads the store's change marker, so while an Ignite store is unreachable those","+fetches fail with `FETCHER_INITIALIZATION_EXCEPTION`; fetchers from the config file are unaffected."," "," Enable these only for trusted callers over a secured channel:"," "],"additions":11,"deletions":5,"truncated":false},{"path":"tika-